<title>SINGAPORE: Wing Tai year net profit up 73 percent.</title>
<headline>Wing Tai year net profit up 73 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in millions of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			145.08  vs   83.93</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	    25.66  vs   14.90</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		  5.00  vs    5.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			  572.95  vs  373.99</p>
<p>    Investment income		 0.04  vs    0.59</p>
<p>    Other &amp; interest income	 8.82  vs    6.90</p>
<p>    Operating profit		238.41  vs  141.59</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)	     17.53  vs   11.15</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  216.21  vs  125.27</p>
<p>    Income from associates	 23.94  vs   17.11</p>
<p>    Tax				  67.40  vs   46.95</p>
<p>    Minorities (expense)	   27.67  vs   11.50</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  (loss) 2.44  vs   50.21 (gain)</p>
<p>Note - Wing Tai Holdings Ltd is a diversified property developer.</p>
<p>--  Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
